/*
:name: removed_spawn_statement
:type: error
:error: expected newline or ';' to end the statement
*/

// The STATEMENT form (removed_spawn.prp pins the call form). `spawn`/`join`/
// `cancel` are gone (docs/pyrope/09-verification.md): a testbench is one
// deterministic `tick`/`step` loop. The pinned grammar no longer has a spawn
// statement, so the front end refuses it as a syntax error at this line instead
// of minting the empty sim-only comb it once did (0 errors, body never lowered).
test spawn_removed {
  spawn job = { assert(true) }  // locate_error_here
}
